   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of partnerships formed for product development and delivery through value chains</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This indicator measures the number of partnerships formed to develop climate risk insurance products. These partnerships should have all different elements in place. The elements that contribute to effectiveness of these partnerships include, 

Reinsurer that provides financial backing and risk-sharing capabilities.
Insurer who underwrites and sells the insurance policies to end customers.
Intermediary who facilitates the distribution and sale of insurance policies.
Digital payment solution that enables efficient and secure payment transactions.
Value chain players who Involve relevant stakeholders within the value chain to ensure product relevance and impact.
Link to adaptation and productivity initiative which Connects the insurance product to broader climate adaptation and productivity goals.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2025-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="3"></target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
