   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of business cases for agricultural insurance products and socialized with stakeholders</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This indicator tracks the number of distinct agricultural insurance product concepts or proposals that have been developed, presented, or discussed with relevant stakeholders, such as farmers, government officials, or insurance providers.


Business Cases: These are detailed analyses and proposals that outline the feasibility, benefits, and costs of agricultural insurance products tailored for specific regions and crops vulnerable to climate risks. The business cases should include assessments of how gender dynamics affect insurance needs and access, and how insurance can be effectively delivered through value chains.

Agricultural Insurance Products: These are insurance solutions designed to mitigate the financial risks associated with climate change impacts on agriculture, particularly in regions and crops identified as high priority.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2026-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="2"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
